vscode: eight clicks and eight Deletes in one very long line
open: retry-ids.ts

@brief
A generator has emitted this array with doubled commas — eight pairs, one
extra comma in each. Delete the spare.

Find the first, delete it, then `;.` your way to the end of the line.

@keys
| `f,` | forward to the next comma |
| `x` | delete the character under the cursor |
| `;` | next comma |
| `.` | delete again |

@hints
Two keys to start, two keys per pair after that.
--
Keep alternating. Stop when the line stops changing — `f` never leaves the
line, so `;` will simply refuse to move once the last pair is done.

@solution
    f,x   then  ;.  seven times

The point of the drill is the pause you are not taking. `;.` is a single
motion of the hand, and after eight of them in a row it should feel like
holding down a key rather than issuing sixteen commands.

Whenever you find yourself about to fix the same small thing several times
along one line, this is the shape to reach for first.

@start retry-ids.ts
export const RETRY_IDS = ['ORD-1182',,'ORD-1183',,'ORD-1184',,'ORD-1185',,'ORD-1186',,'ORD-1187',,'ORD-1188',,'ORD-1189',,'ORD-1190'];

